MID_SE_Lor_Set_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_001: Hm? Is that Loretta? What is she doing all alone?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_002: Loretta, it's very late to be wandering around.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_003: Eeek! It's a monster!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_004: A monster? Where?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_005: That's a trick of shadows from the foliage swaying in\nthe wind.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_006: There is no monster here, I assure you.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_007: N-no! Get away from me!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_008: Why are you scared of me? Do you think I'm some\nkind of monster?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_009: Calm yourself, Loretta. I am no such creature.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_010: Stay back! Someone, help me! Where are you, Ozin?!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_011: Now then, as you can see, I am no monster.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_012: Um, yeah. S-sorry about that.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_013: I was taken aback, but I'm fine. Your confusion was\nunderstandable—it's very dark out.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_014: Anyway, you should get some rest. I'd be happy to\nread you a bedtime story.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_015: Save it, OK? You don't need to treat me like a kid.\nAnd while we're on the subject...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_016: I don't want you going around telling people I was\njumping at shadows.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_017: Can I bribe you to keep your mouth shut?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_018: I have no need of money, I— Is this...dried fruit?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_019: They're coffee beans. Better than you'd think\nto chew on!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_020: Haha. I see. So this is the bribe, hm? Mmmm.\nIndeed, these are tasty.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_C_021: Don't you worry. I won't tell anyone—you have\nmy word.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_001: Hey. You better not have told anyone about\nyou-know-what.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_002: Hm? Oh, you mean about the scare from that night.\nI haven't whispered it to a soul.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_003: You bribed me for my silence, so silent I remained.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_004: That's right. Although it kinda seemed like you'd\nforgotten all about it.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_005: I was intentionally putting it out of my mind.\nRecalling that night wounds me a bit.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_006: You thought I was a monster, after all. Did I truly\nlook so horrifying?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_007: You can be pretty scary-looking. It might be the\nmerciless vibes you give off.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_008: Merciless...vibes? Is that how you see me?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_009: I'm not saying I was right! It's an easy mistake to\nmake in the dark.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_010: Especially since I'm terrified of monsters and stuff.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_011: I used to have this dream where...tons of...and\nall started... It was horrifying.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_012: A dream about what? I couldn't quite hear you.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_013: I SAID, I used to have this— Y'know what, forget it.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_014: Well now I'm even more curious.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_015: I'm telling you, it's nothing. I didn't have any dreams,\nand I never said anything about them.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_016: There's no need for dishonesty... But if you're\nembarrassed, I won't force you to share.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_017: Who said I was embarrassed?! Ugh, fine...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_018: You kept my secret, so I might as well. Bend over\nand I'll whisper it in your ear.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_019: Apologies, but perhaps there's another way to\ntell me?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_020: How else can I keep it quiet if I don't whisper?\nC'mon, gimme your ear!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_021: Please! You shouldn't cross lines like that!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_022: Like what? You wanted to know, so I'm gonna\ntell you!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_023: Whoa! Your ears are so...pointy. Are you\nsome kinda...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_030: Whoa! Your ears are so...pointy. But I guess that\nmakes sense, huh.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_024: Well, there's nothing to be done about it now.\nHere—have some Fódlan tea leaves as a bribe.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_025: This is called crescent-moon tea. Like the soft light of\nthe moon, the taste itself is quite soft.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_026: My daughter loves it. I hope you enjoy it as well.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_027: Oh yeah? Thanks.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_028: Don't worry. I won't blab to anybody.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_B_029: Then we have a deal. Let's keep these\nunderstandings strictly confidential.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_001: Whatcha doing? Going for a walk? For fun?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_002: Indeed. Leisurely strolls give me time to ponder what\nmy next fable might be.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_003: "Fable"? What's that?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_004: It's a story that contains a moral lesson. I enjoy\nwriting them as a hobby.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_005: Huh. Doesn't sound fun to me, but\neveryone's different.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_006: She's grown fond of me. It's hard to imagine she\nthought I was a monster, once upon a time.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_007: Hm? Oh, there's a flock of birds over there. Lemme\nget rid of 'em for you.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_008: Is that really necessary? They don't look particularly\ndangerous...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_009: OK, the birds are gone. But stay sharp! There's a\nstone at your feet.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_010: You smart guys might die if you trip, right?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_011: What are you talking about? A little stumble wouldn't\nkill me...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_012: Well, it's still better not to trip. Someone might notice\nyour ears when you're sprawled out.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_013: That much is true, I suppose. Thank you for\nyour concern.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_014: No problem. We've both got our secrets.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_015: And I'll make sure they STAY secret.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_016: I see—that's why you've been so vigilant about\nmy surroundings.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_017: Yeah. We're like a two-member secret-keeping club.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_018: You know, I still don't understand why it is you're so\nafraid of monsters...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_019: Oh yeah, we never got around to that part. You don't\nmind lending me your ear now, right?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_020: Not at all, now that you know my secret. OK, go\nahead and whisper it to me.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_021: Will do. Just don't laugh, OK?
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_022: A while ago, I used to have these terrible dreams.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_023: In them, I was surrounded by a whole horde of\nbaby chicks. They were all pecking at me.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_024: It was cute at first. But then they got bigger...and\nbigger...and made these creepy noises. It was awful.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_025: Eh...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_026: What's that look for? Speak up.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_027: I... I am so sorry... Hahaha!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_028: Augh! Hey! I told you not to laugh!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_029: My apologies! Ahaha... You mentioned birds in your\ndream, and you are so wary of birds, and... Hahaha!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_030: This is another good reason to hate monsters.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_031: I do apologize, sincerely—but I do not understand\nyour fear of birds.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_032: Wipe that smirk off your face! If I hadn't mistaken\nyou for a monster, this would never have happened.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_033: Honestly, what freaked me out then was how the\nswaying branches looked like a huge bird's feathers.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_034: Ah, so I appeared like a bird monster to you. Well,\nthat interaction was the start of our friendship.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_035: C'mon, let's get back to our walk. You were\npondering or whatever for your fable stuff.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_036: Come to think of it, we could turn our own little story\ninto a proper fable.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_037: What? You can't seriously mean...
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_038: Of course I can. I think it would make for an\nexcellent fable. I'll begin writing it immediately.
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_039: Ughhh! First I get laughed at, and now he's gonna\nmake a fable out of me!
MID_SE_Lor_Set_A_040: I'll never forgive you, monsters!